# Make the orc warrior every A_DEQU check uses, and freeze the monsters.
# Included by dequ-hardness-plain.keys, dequ-hardness-magic.keys,
# dequ-reach.keys, dequ-sunder.keys and dequ-owner-resist.keys.
#
# The character is a male orc WARRIOR, neutral, worshipping whichever god the
# game offers. A warrior is deliberate: he starts with a weapon in hand, and
# every one of these checks is about what happens to a weapon. The sequence is
# tools/keys/dequ-save-message.keys's chargen, which is known to reach the
# wizard menu on seed 5 under tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat.
#
# Every choice here is a menu letter, and menu letters move when the list
# changes. Run with a fixed seed or the attribute rolls change, the offered
# feats change with them, and these letters choose something else.
#
# Freeze Monsters is on so a summoned monster neither moves nor takes a turn of
# its own. It still ANSWERS a blow -- A_DEQU fires from inside the resolution of
# the player's own attack -- which is the whole point of these checks.

a       # Initial Choices: [a] Create a New Character
n       # Alter the character generation options? -- no
y       # Explore Mode -- yes
i       # Race:  [i] Orc
a       # Subrace: [a] Orc (Standard)
j       # Class: [j] Warrior -- starts with a weapon in hand
a       # Attributes: the first offered set
c       # Alignment: [c] Neutral
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
@while "wish to worship" y
@while "Choose a Domain" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Focus on which Weapon" a
@while "|  *" RIGHT RIGHT RIGHT DOWN
ENTER y
a       # Personality archetype
@until "Things in View" ESC

# 'w' opens wizard mode and 'y' confirms it the first time. The pair is driven
# by @until rather than written out, because a keystroke swallowed by a prompt
# that was still up would spend every key after it on the wrong thing.
@until "Wizard Mode Options" w y
w       # [w] Wizard Mode Switches
# The switch list draws no cursor a screen dump can see, so this counts rows:
# Freeze Monsters is the eleventh, and the cursor opens on the first.
DOWN*10
SPACE   # Freeze Monsters: NO -> YES
ESC
